'Exact Parseval identity for the finite transform','The squared Haar coefficients sum to the original squared data norm. For the stated gap vector the energy is65, decomposed as441/8 at the coarsest mean,9/8 at the coarsest detail,9/4 at the next details and13/2 at the finest details.',
'For each pair, ((a+b)/√2)²+((a−b)/√2)²=a²+b². Every recursive stage is therefore orthogonal and preserves total squared norm. The initial energy is1+4+4+16+4+16+4+16=65. The first-stage details are−1/√2,−2/√2,−2/√2,−2/√2, whose squared sum is13/2. The next-stage details are−3/2 and0, contributing9/4. The final detail is−3/(2√2), contributing9/8, while the final average is21/(2√2), contributing441/8. Adding these rational energies gives(441+9+18+52)/8=65. The computation is exact even if floating-point square roots are used for a visual display.',
'Compare the genuine gap vector with any permutation of its entries.',
'Every permutation has the same total energy65 and the same coarsest mean, but its scale details generally change because adjacency changes. Consequently a histogram or marginal gap distribution cannot determine a wavelet spectrum. A synthetic sequence can be matched to one statistic while disagreeing in another.',
'The transform certifies finite scale-dependent structure in a specified sequence. The provenance of the data is part of the statement.',
'No infinite limiting wavelet law, prime-gap conjecture or quantum interpretation follows from eight gaps. The historical source did not recover an implemented transform or genuine prime-data conclusion.',
