['LetΦ:R→R² beΦ(x)=(x²,x³). Its image satisfiesv²=u³ andu≥0.','The inverse isx=v/u whenu>0, withx=0 at(u,v)=(0,0).'],
'Injectivity and inverse instability','Φ is injective. It is a homeomorphism onto the real cusp, but its inverse is not locally Lipschitz at the origin. In polynomial coordinate rings,C[t²,t³] is strictly smaller than its normalizationC[t].',
