'Their squared coordinates coincide, while cubic coordinates differ by2ε³. Thus||Φ(ε)−Φ(−ε)||=2|ε|³ even though their input distance is2|ε|. Withε=1/10 the feature distance is1/500 and the input distance1/5. The cubic coordinate preserves the sign exactly in noiseless arithmetic but becomes extremely small near zero.',
'Injectivity does not guarantee a well-conditioned feature representation. The derivativeΦ′(0)=(0,0) explains the local loss of sensitivity.',
